description:
Foundational sub-bead. Extracts Commonplace.Process.Orchestrator's compile core (apps/commonplace/lib/commonplace/process/orchestrator.ex:283-340) into a substrate-tier primitive. Generalizes for ComputeSpec + future consumers.

API:
- read(uuid, store) → {:ok, source_string, content_hash} | {:error, reason}
- compile(uuid, store) → {:ok, module_atom} | {:error, reason}  
- resolve(ref, context_uuid, store) → {:ok, module_atom} | {:error, reason}

Two-ETS-table cache (round-1 audit (A)):
- :source_doc_index — {uuid → content_hash}
- :source_doc_cache — {content_hash → module_atom}
Compile flow: lookup latest hash for uuid; if same as current content hash, return cached module; if different, purge old module + delete old entries + compile + insert new. O(1) stale cleanup, no leak.

Internals:
- Code.compile_string(source, filename) — filename is 'docref://' <> uuid for stacktrace debuggability
- :code.purge(module_atom) before each compile (BEAM old/current discipline; same as Orchestrator)
- Module name comes from source's defmodule line (held #2 α — source self-names)

Moduledoc carries worked end-to-end example (round-1 audit (C)) — show what _renderer.ex source looks like with Commonplace.UserCode.<Domain>.<Name> convention.

Lands first; (i.5) and (ii) and (iii) parallel-claimable after (i).

Caller-facing API Merger.merge(L, R, strategy: :translate | :merge_snapshot, opts). No automatic heuristics — caller chooses strategy. Red events:
- [:commonplace, :merge, :completed] %{strategy, L, R, result_id}
- [:commonplace, :merge, :failed] %{strategy, reason, L, R}

Includes opt-in fallback to positional rebase (reusing 6.6 machinery) for edges where translation fails.

Depends on 7.3, 7.4.

@dump with no target dumps the room (works); @dump <obj> resolves obj in scope (works); @dump here returns 'Can't find here.' Workspace expects 'here'/'room' to be a parser shortcut for current room (parallel to @desc / @name which both accept 'here').

Fix: in dispatch_builder('@dump', cmd, ctx) — if cmd.target in ['here', 'room'], render the room. Tiny patch.

Linked to CX-v55j umbrella as P1-followup.
